<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ClickHouse's default config listens on `::`. A Docker bridge network without IPv6
  rejects that, and the server logs one of these per port:

    Listen [::]:8123 failed: DNS error: EAI: Address family for hostname not supported

  Every listener fails, so 8123 never opens, the container healthcheck against
  localhost:8123/ping can never succeed, and the container stays "unhealthy"
  forever. Anything gated on it through depends_on goes down with it: here that is
  signoz-query-service and signoz-otel-collector, i.e. the whole observability half
  of the demo.

  It presents as a slow start, which is misleading. It is not slow; the port is
  never bound. ClickHouse's own error message recommends this exact override.

  Note for future edits: an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen, so don't
  write CLI flags in here. Doing that turned this file into a startup crash loop.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <listen_host>0.0.0.0</listen_host>
</clickhouse>
